MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_001: Oh, you poor thing... Are you really feeling that\nunwell? The wind is dry, I agree...
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_002: Oho! Could it be— You're conversing with spirits,\naren't you!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_003: You can hear them too, Peppe? Sense them,\nfeel them?
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_004: We cannot! We are a king, unable to do that\nwhich our shamans can!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_005: But you can do something that no one in Brigid\ncan—exchange words with the spirits!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_006: Oh... I thought they would be so happy to have\nanother person to talk to.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_007: We are gladdened by this discovery! Few in this\nland of gods even know of the spirits!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_008: Those here who use spirit magic commune with\nthem only for selfish need. Such disrespect.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_009: I share the same opinion—very much the same.\nI think of them as my friends.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_010: Ninae, tell me... The spirits... Are they still with us,\neven at this moment?
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_011: Yes, they are. Right at your side, and right in\nfront of you.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_012: O guiding spirits... We give thanks for the\nblessings you bestow on us.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_013: We are with you, as you are with us. We pledge\nour protection, that you may bless us forever.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_014: Ah... The spirits are happy.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_015: Really and truly? Then our voice reached them.\nThat is all that matters.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_016: The words you just spoke... Was that a prayer\nfrom your country?
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_017: We were saying one of Brigid's most traditional\nprayers, though abridged from the full ritual.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_018: In it, we praise the bond between spirits and\nhumans, reminding ourselves of its eternal sanctity.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_019: I thought...I knew much about the spirits.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_020: But I've never known that something like that\nwould make them happy.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_021: Peppe, please... Tell me more about the spirits.\nI sense now there's so much I don't know.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_C_022: We will suspend our studies! You can consider the\nking of Brigid your personal tutor in this matter!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_001: Now...we believe that an ocean spirit shows us two\nfaces. One that is merciful, granting blessings.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_002: And one that is terrifying, bringing disaster. Do you\ngrasp the dual nature of what we are saying?
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_003: Yes... Yes, I do. You have a lot of spirits that are\npart of Brigid life, don't you?
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_004: A spirit of the ocean, and one of the forest... Also\nthe spirits of the sky and of trees...
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_005: Fascinating! Utterly! I've never been able to\ndiscuss any of this in such depth.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_006: Ninae... We would like to hear your story.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_007: We wish to know when—and how—you learned to\ncommune with the spirits like you do.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_008: The "how" might relate to my father's blood.\nI don't know the "when" of the "how."
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_009: I know only that one day I noticed them talking.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_010: We see... So, this isn't something that can be\ntaught, at least not easily. Hmm...
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_011: Ninae! We envy you!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_012: Envy...me?
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_013: In our country, we believe that the spirits are all\naround us—and we do pray to them.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_014: We revere them and know they protect us. We live\nour lives with them, yet they are beyond us.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_015: If only my people could converse with them. They\nwould find great and joyful meaning in that.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_016: A pitiful situation, I understand... But, Peppe, if\nyou ever want to speak to the spirits...
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_017: you can always ask me to help.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_018: Wh-what? You mean, whenever we want?
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_019: I'll share your words with them, and then their\nwords with you.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_020: Incredible! You would be the king's interpreter? Your\nnobility shines brightly, offering this!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_021: Although...our greater wish is to speak with the\nspirits of our homeland, not just those of Dagda.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_022: Then I'll travel to Brigid. I would like to meet the\nspirits there too—each and every one of them.
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_023: You would cross the ocean for this? How dutiful,\nadmirable, and commendable!
MID_SE_Nin_Pep_B_024: We hereby invite you to Brigid as our most honored\nguest! We would dearly like to see you visit, Ninae!